# P6 — provider-agnostic LLM transport

## Context

After the Apps and Lakebase work, OntoBricks runs on any container against any
Postgres — but its agents still only talked to a Databricks workspace. One line
was the whole coupling:

```python
url = f"{host.rstrip('/')}/serving-endpoints/{endpoint_name}/invocations"
```

That is `src/agents/engine_base.py:84`, the single LLM transport for all 11 agent
engines. Databricks serving endpoints already speak the OpenAI chat-completions
request and response shape, so only two things actually differ between providers:
the URL, and whether the model name travels in the body. This change moves both
behind one resolver and keeps the **Databricks Foundation Model API as a preset**,
not a requirement.

Gated by `.cursor/12-ai-feature-lifecycle.mdc`, so it went SPEC → dataset → red
tests → implementation → eval, in that order.

## Changes

1. **`.planning/agents/engine_base/SPEC.md`** (new) — the design. Records why the
   eval is contract-shaped rather than judge-scored, why the 11 engine signatures
   deliberately do *not* change, and §11, the gate hole found while writing it.

2. **`.planning/agents/engine_base/PLAN.md`** (new) — brainstorm decisions, the
   Fowler smells addressed, the steps, and an explicit "Not done" section.

3. **`tests/eval/datasets/engine_base/baseline.jsonl`** (new, 24 rows) and
   **`regression.jsonl`** (new, 3 rows) — hand-curated transport-contract cases.
   Each row is a `(env, host, token, endpoint_name)` input and the exact expected
   URL, `Authorization` header and `model`-key presence. Written and run **red
   (109 failures) before any source change**, so they are known to bind to real
   behaviour rather than to whatever the implementation happened to do.

4. **`src/shared/config/LLMTarget.py`** (new, 213 lines) — resolves where to POST
   and in which dialect. Pure config, no I/O, so the transport keeps its single
   responsibility. Sits beside `RuntimeEnv` and `TraversalLimits`, the other two
   env-derived config classes from this workstream.

5. **`src/agents/engine_base.py`** — URL, headers and the `model` body field now
   come from the resolver. `call_serving_endpoint`'s signature is untouched, so all
   11 engines and the 12 test modules that patch it by name are untouched too.

6. **`src/back/core/sqlwizard/SQLWizardService.py`** — the same invocations URL was
   hardcoded a *second* time here (`:286`), which the P6 scope as originally
   written would have missed. Now shares the resolver.
   `get_model_serving_endpoints` returns the configured models when there is no
   workspace to enumerate, so the Domain Settings picker is never empty.

7. **`src/back/core/helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py`** — `require_serving_llm`
   delegates the decision to `LLMTarget.resolve`, so a route can never admit a
   request the transport would then refuse. It stops demanding Databricks
   credentials when an external provider is configured, while still returning
   them (possibly empty) because agent *tools* use them for Unity Catalog reads.

8. **`src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`** — three routes (700, 2204, 2356) each
   carried the same 12-line "require credentials, else auto-discover, else fail"
   block. **Extract Function** `_require_llm`; each site is now one line.
   `_auto_discover_llm_endpoint` short-circuits on a configured external provider,
   which otherwise returned nothing because there is no Databricks client to ask.

9. **`src/api/routers/internal/mapping.py`** — the LLM-endpoints picker route no
   longer refuses when there is no workspace client but a provider is configured.

10. **`tests/eval/judges/contract.py`** (new) — the rule-based judge, shared
    between the pytest suite and the eval runner so the gate and the tests cannot
    disagree about what passing means.

11. **`tests/units/agents/test_engine_base_transport_contract.py`** (new, 112
    tests) — the dataset as a unit test, so a contract regression fails in
